.TH INZONE-PROFILE 1 "2026-10-04" "inzone-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inzone-profile \- manage INZONE audio profiles and headset controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inzone-profile
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inzone-profile
opens the terminal interface when invoked without arguments in an interactive
terminal. Commands can select an audio profile, adjust DSP settings, inspect
headset state, and configure process-based automatic profile switching.
.PP
Run this command as the desktop user. Profile activation updates user audio
configuration and applies the requested routing and DSP settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B --help, -h, --list
Print the complete command and option reference.
.TP
.B --tui
Open the terminal interface.
.TP
.B --gui
Launch the Qt desktop interface.
.TP
.B fps, music, voice, balanced, surround
Activate the named built-in profile. A custom profile identifier can also be
supplied as the command.
.TP
.B restore
Restore the original audio configuration saved by user setup.
.TP
.B --status
Print the active profile identifier.
.TP
.B --profiles
List built-in and custom profiles.
.TP
.B --settings
Print saved DSP settings.
.TP
.BI "--set " "PROFILE KEY JSON_VALUE"
Change and apply a DSP option. Supported keys include
.BR drc ,
.BR output_alc ,
.BR mic_agc ,
.BR hrtf ,
.BR eq ,
.BR eq_enable ,
.BR sound_mode ,
and
.BR base_eq .
Boolean options use JSON
.B true
or
.BR false .
.TP
.B --device-status
Read headset state, including available firmware version information.
.TP
.BI "--device-set " "FIELD VALUE"
Set a supported headset field and verify its readback.
.TP
.B --auto-config
Print application profile association rules.
.TP
.BI "--auto-bind " "APP PROFILE " [ PRIORITY ]
Add or replace a process-based profile association.
.TP
.BI "--auto-remove " APP
Remove an application association.
.TP
.B --auto-enable, --auto-disable
Enable or disable automatic switching through the user service.
.TP
.B --auto-watch
Run the process association watcher in the foreground. The user service uses
this command for background automatic switching.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable command and DSP verification logging. This flag can accompany another
command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/inzone-h9-ii/
User profile, DSP, and automation configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/inzone-linux/
Separately acquired DSP assets and personal filter data.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/inzone-linux/debug.log
Diagnostic log when debug mode is enabled.
.SH SETUP
Use
.BR inzone-tools (1)
to initialize the desktop user's configuration before the first profile switch.
Firmware update operations are not provided.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inzone-gui (1),
.BR inzone-tools (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
